<!-- ══ COMPETITIVE MOATS ══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="sec-label">The 6 Competitive Moats — Why No One Can Copy This</div>
  <div class="sec-head">Category creation is the first-mover advantage. The moats compound over time.</div>
  <div class="moats">
    <div class="moat"><div class="moat-num">01</div><div class="moat-title">Original Data Creation</div><div class="moat-body">Generates private intelligence through therapeutic conversation. Every competitor only monitors what already exists publicly. Different in kind, not just quantity. Cannot be scraped, purchased, or accessed from any other source.</div></div>
    <div class="moat"><div class="moat-num">02</div><div class="moat-title">Proprietary Dataset</div><div class="moat-body">Owned by BISS and unavailable anywhere else. Cannot be replicated or licensed from any third party. Grows with every conversation — creating an exponentially widening gap.</div></div>
    <div class="moat"><div class="moat-num">03</div><div class="moat-title">Network Effects</div><div class="moat-body">More stories → richer intelligence → more value → better product → more users. Self-reinforcing at every level and accelerates with scale in a way that cannot be replicated by any standalone tool.</div></div>
    <div class="moat"><div class="moat-num">04</div><div class="moat-title">Technology Barriers</div><div class="moat-body">Real-time emotional AI, behavioral biometrics, multi-brand story splitting. Months of specialized development. The therapeutic interface is a product philosophy, not a feature that can simply be added.</div></div>
    <div class="moat"><div class="moat-num">05</div><div class="moat-title">Content Creator Loyalty</div><div class="moat-body">Free users loyal because they receive genuine therapeutic value — not because they're locked in. Sustainable loyalty that generates word-of-mouth. The emotional value of the platform is psychologically irreplaceable.</div></div>
    <div class="moat"><div class="moat-num">06</div><div class="moat-title">Category Leadership Window</div><div class="moat-body">18–24 months to establish dominance. Once BISS defines Conversational Customer Intelligence and owns it in the market's mind, displacement requires reframing the entire category.</div></div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ══ LAUNCH STRATEGY ════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="sec-label">Launch Strategy — From Southern California to Global Category Leadership</div>
  <div class="sec-body">BISS launches hyperlocal, proves product-market fit, then expands. The cold start problem is solved through four-phase sequencing: content seeding with travel bloggers, influencer test accounts, business prompt seeding, then organic community growth.</div>
  <table class="launch-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Phase</th><th>Geography &amp; Timing</th><th>Categories &amp; Verticals</th><th>ARR Target</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Alpha</td><td>Southern California · Year 1–2</td><td>Travel (Airlines, Lodging) + Restaurants (QSR, Fast Casual)</td><td>$3.5K–$29K</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Beta</td><td>National · Year 2–3</td><td>Car Rentals, Casual &amp; Full-Service Dining added</td><td>$79K</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Growth</td><td>US National · Year 3</td><td>Retail, Entertainment. Data licensing begins. Series A.</td><td>$150–250K</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Scale</td><td>US + UK + Australia · Year 4–5</td><td>Healthcare, Automotive, Financial Services, E-Commerce</td><td>$8–12M</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<!-- ══ STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIPS — full PDF image ═══════════════ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="sec-label">Strategic Partnerships — The First Ten Travel Relationships</div>
  <div class="visual-full"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="BISS Strategic Partnerships — The First Ten"></div>
  <div class="visual-caption">Strategic Partnerships — Alpha &amp; Beta phases · From official BISS Platform Narrative</div>
</div>

<div class="divider"></div>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     WIREFRAME SHOWCASE — All 6 screens from the wireframes session
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="sec-label">Product Wireframes — The BISS Experience Designed</div>
  <div class="sec-head">Six screens. Every layer of the platform, from first conversation to B2B intelligence.</div>
  <div class="sec-body">These wireframes were designed to tell the BISS story in the order that matters — starting with the core magic (therapeutic AI + emotional face), through the content output, brand intelligence, community, and finally the contest platform. Built with the BISS design token system: teal for trust/positive, gold for authentic/earned, coral/red for negative/pain, sky blue for data/B2B.</div>
</div>

<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<!-- SCREEN 1: AI CHAT + EMOTIONAL FACE                       -->
<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="wf-screen">
  <div class="wf-header">
    <div class="wf-title">Screen 01 — AI Chat + Emotional Face</div>
    <div class="wf-num">The Core Experience</div>
  </div>
  <div class="wf-desc">The entry point. The AI asks a single open-ended question and the Real-Time Emotional Face mirrors the user's emotional state as they type. Brand detection happens automatically — no dropdowns, no forms. This screen is the entire onboarding experience: no tutorial needed.</div>
  <div class="wf-body">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:start">
      <div class="phone-outer">
        <div class="phone-frame">
          <div class="phone-status"><span>9:41</span><span style="display:flex;gap:4px;align-items:center"><span style="font-size:10px">●●●●</span><span>WiFi</span><span>🔋</span></span></div>
          <div class="phone-nav">
            <span style="font-size:13px;color:#555">← Back</span>
            <span style="font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:var(--pink);letter-spacing:1px">BISS</span>
            <span style="font-size:13px;color:#555">···</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Emotional Face Zone -->
          <div style="background:#0d1117;padding:20px 0 14px;text-align:center;border-bottom:.5px solid #1e2030">
            <div style="font-size:9px;color:#444;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:10px">Reading your story...</div>
            <!-- Face SVG -->
            <svg width="72" height="72" viewBox="0 0 72 72" style="display:block;margin:0 auto">
              <circle cx="36" cy="36" r="34" fill="#1a2035" stroke="#2a3050" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              <!-- Frustrated expression -->
              <ellipse cx="24" cy="30" rx="5" ry="5.5" fill="#00C4A7" opacity=".9"/>
              <ellipse cx="48" cy="30" rx="5" ry="5.5" fill="#00C4A7" opacity=".9"/>
              <!-- Furrowed brows -->
              <path d="M18 24 Q24 21 30 24" stroke="#F97066" stroke-width="2" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              <path d="M42 24 Q48 21 54 24" stroke="#F97066" stroke-width="2" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              <!-- Downturned mouth -->
              <path d="M25 48 Q36 42 47 48" stroke="#F97066" stroke-width="2.5" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
            <div style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;background:#1e2030;border:.5px solid #2a2a3a;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-top:8px">
              <span style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:#F97066;display:inline-block"></span>frustrated
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- Chat messages -->
          <div style="padding:14px 14px 0;background:#0d1117">
            <div class="chat-ai">Tell me about a recent experience you've had with any brand, product, or service.</div>
            <div class="chat-user">My Delta flight to NYC was delayed 3 hours — they never explained anything and I missed my mom's birthday dinner</div>
            <div style="margin-top:6px">
              <div class="chat-pill">✈ Delta → 1 journal detected</div>
            </div>
            <div class="chat-ai" style="margin-top:10px">That sounds incredibly frustrating — especially with the personal stakes of your mom's birthday. How did the gate staff handle it when you asked for updates?</div>
          </div>
          <!-- Input -->
          <div style="padding:10px 14px 14px;background:#0d1117">
            <div style="background:#1a2035;border:.5px solid #2a3050;border-radius:24px;padding:10px 14px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center">
              <span style="font-size:12px;color:#3a5070">Share your experience...</span>
              <span style="width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--teal);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:14px;color:#0d1117;font-weight:700">↑</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- Tab Bar -->
          <div class="phone-tab-bar">
            <div class="phone-tab"><span style="font-size:18px">⌂</span>Home</div>
            <div class="phone-tab"><span style="font-size:18px">⊕</span>Explore</div>
            <div class="phone-tab active"><span style="font-size:22px;color:var(--pink)">+</span></div>
            <div class="phone-tab"><span style="font-size:18px">◎</span>Brands</div>
            <div class="phone-tab"><span style="font-size:18px">◯</span>Profile</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Annotations -->
      <div style="padding:8px 0">
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px"><span style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--teal);color:var(--dark);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0">1</span><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--white)">Emotional Face</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding-left:34px">Reacts in real time as the user types. Expression shifts from neutral → frustrated → angry → relieved. Not an avatar — it's a mirror. In a real build this pulses between expressions as sentiment shifts in the text, which is the moment people screenshot and share.</div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px"><span style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--teal);color:var(--dark);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0">2</span><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--white)">Contextual AI Follow-up</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding-left:34px">The AI detected personal stakes ("mom's birthday") and probed deeper. No survey has ever done this. Contextual, not scripted — the follow-up changes based on what the user actually said.</div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px"><span style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--teal);color:var(--dark);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0">3</span><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--white)">Brand Detection Pill</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding-left:34px">Appears automatically as soon as a brand is mentioned. Tells the user their story is being captured for Delta specifically. More brands mentioned = more pills. This is the moment they see the platform "working."</div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--card2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:12px 14px">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:600;color:var(--teal);letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px">Non-negotiables on this screen</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7">No star rating input · AI-inferred sentiment only<br>No brand dropdown — natural language detection<br>Profanity cleaned, never deleted (full vowel-masking)<br>Real name never displayed — pseudonym only<br>No tutorial screen — just talk, BISS does the rest</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<!-- SCREEN 2: JOURNAL ENTRY                                  -->
<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="wf-screen">
  <div class="wf-header">
    <div class="wf-title">Screen 02 — Journal Entry / Story Card</div>
    <div class="wf-num">The Content Output</div>
  </div>
  <div class="wf-desc">The output of the AI conversation. One messy conversation becomes a polished, published journal entry with AI-inferred sentiment score, brand attribution, privacy controls, and XP earned. This is the user's "public diary" — the content layer that powers everything else on the platform.</div>
  <div class="wf-body">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:start">
      <div class="phone-outer">
        <div class="phone-frame">
          <div class="phone-status"><span>9:41</span><span>🔋</span></div>
          <div class="phone-nav">
            <span style="font-size:13px;color:#555">← Back</span>
            <span style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0">Journal Entry</span>
            <span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--teal)">Share</span>
          </div>
          <div style="padding:16px 14px;background:#0d1117">
            <!-- Brand + AI Score header -->
            <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:10px">
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px">
                <div style="width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:8px;background:#1a2035;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:14px;color:#ccc">✈</div>
                <div>
                  <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0">Delta Airlines</div>
                  <div style="font-size:10px;color:#3a5070">Airlines · Travel</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div style="text-align:right">
                <div style="font-family:'Syne',sans-serif;font-size:28px;font-weight:800;color:#F97066;line-height:1">2.8</div>
                <div style="font-size:9px;color:#3a5070">AI inferred · no star rating</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <!-- Story title -->
            <div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0;margin-bottom:8px;line-height:1.3">"The Three-Hour Delta Nightmare"</div>
            <!-- Story text -->
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:#8a9abc;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px">I arrived two hours early for my NYC flight. No updates for 90 minutes. No explanations at the gate. Missed my connection, which meant missing my mom's birthday dinner — an event she'd been planning for months...</div>
            <!-- Sentiment bar -->
            <div style="margin-bottom:12px">
              <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:10px;color:#3a5070;margin-bottom:4px"><span>Sentiment</span><span style="color:#F97066">Negative</span></div>
              <div style="height:6px;background:#1a2540;border-radius:3px;overflow:hidden"><div style="width:20%;height:100%;background:#F97066;border-radius:3px"></div></div>
            </div>
            <!-- Tags -->
            <div style="display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:12px">
              <span style="background:#1a2035;border:.5px solid #2a3050;border-radius:12px;padding:3px 8px;font-size:10px;color:#647a96">Delay</span>
              <span style="background:#1a2035;border:.5px solid #2a3050;border-radius:12px;padding:3px 8px;font-size:10px;color:#647a96">Communication</span>
              <span style="background:#1a2035;border:.5px solid #2a3050;border-radius:12px;padding:3px 8px;font-size:10px;color:#647a96">Gate Service</span>
            </div>
            <!-- Privacy + XP row -->
            <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;background:#0a1220;border-radius:8px;padding:8px 10px;margin-bottom:10px">
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-size:11px;color:#3a5070"><span>🔒</span>Public · PinkWagon77</div>
              <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--teal)">+40 XP earned</div>
            </div>
            <!-- One-word responses -->
            <div style="font-size:10px;color:#3a5070;margin-bottom:6px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px">Community responses</div>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap">
              <div class="owp">Relatable</div>
              <div class="owp">Ugh</div>
              <div class="owp">Same</div>
              <div class="owp" style="background:#1a3020;border-color:#2a4030;color:var(--teal)">+ Respond</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Annotations -->
      <div style="padding:8px 0">
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px"><span style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--gold);color:var(--dark);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0">1</span><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--white)">AI-Inferred Score (2.8)</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding-left:34px">No star rating — ever. The AI read the full narrative and inferred 2.8 from the emotional content, specific language, and context. Two users with the same terrible experience will get similar scores even if one would give 1 star and another 3.</div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px"><span style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--gold);color:var(--dark);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0">2</span><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--white)">Pseudonymous Identity</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding-left:34px">Published as "PinkWagon77" — never the user's real name. Real identity verified in the backend but never surfaced. This is what makes honest sharing possible at scale.</div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px"><span style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--gold);color:var(--dark);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0">3</span><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--white)">One-Word Response System</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding-left:34px">Community members respond with a single chosen word — not a full comment. Eliminates harassment, pile-ons, and toxicity while creating meaningful emotional signal about how stories land. "Relatable" and "Same" carry more weight than a thumbs-up.</div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--card2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:12px 14px">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:600;color:var(--gold);letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px">What happens in the background</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7">This entry simultaneously feeds:<br>· Delta's B2B intelligence dashboard (real time)<br>· Delta's public Brand Page story feed<br>· The community discovery feed for followed users<br>· BISS's aggregate sentiment dataset</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<!-- SCREEN 3: BRAND PAGE                                     -->
<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="wf-screen">
  <div class="wf-header">
    <div class="wf-title">Screen 03 — Brand Page</div>
    <div class="wf-num">Living Brand Intelligence</div>
  </div>
  <div class="wf-desc">Every brand mentioned on BISS automatically gets a page — built from authentic user stories before any business ever claims it. When a business subscribes, they claim and verify their Brand Page. This is what the consumer sees; the B2B dashboard (Screen 4) shows the business a deeper layer of the same data.</div>
  <div class="wf-body">
    <div class="phone-outer">
      <div class="phone-frame">
        <div class="phone-status"><span>9:41</span><span>🔋</span></div>
        <div style="background:#0d1117;padding:12px 14px 10px;border-bottom:.5px solid #1e2030">
          <div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700;color:#e8e8f0;margin-bottom:2px">Southwest Airlines</div>
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:#3a5070">Airlines · Travel · 847 stories</div>
        </div>
        <!-- Stats row -->
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:0;border-bottom:.5px solid #1e2030">
          <div style="padding:12px;text-align:center;border-right:.5px solid #1e2030">
            <div style="font-family:'Syne',sans-serif;font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:var(--teal)">4.2</div>
            <div style="font-size:10px;color:#3a5070">Sentiment</div>
          </div>
          <div style="padding:12px;text-align:center;border-right:.5px solid #1e2030">
            <div style="font-family:'Syne',sans-serif;font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:var(--teal)">847</div>
            <div style="font-size:10px;color:#3a5070">Stories</div>
          </div>
          <div style="padding:12px;text-align:center">
            <div style="font-family:'Syne',sans-serif;font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:var(--gold)">48</div>
            <div style="font-size:10px;color:#3a5070">NPS Proxy</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Top Pain Points -->
        <div style="padding:12px 14px;border-bottom:.5px solid #1e2030">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:#3a5070;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:8px">Top pain points</div>
          <div class="pain-item"><div class="pain-label"><span>Boarding delays</span><span>73%</span></div><div class="pain-track"><div class="pain-fill" style="width:73%;background:var(--gold)"></div></div></div>
          <div class="pain-item"><div class="pain-label"><span>App reliability</span><span>58%</span></div><div class="pain-track"><div class="pain-fill" style="width:58%;background:var(--gold)"></div></div></div>
          <div class="pain-item"><div class="pain-label"><span>Communication</span><span>40%</span></div><div class="pain-track"><div class="pain-fill" style="width:40%;background:var(--gold)"></div></div></div>
        </div>
        <!-- Recent stories -->
        <div style="padding:12px 14px">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:#3a5070;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:8px">Recent stories</div>
          <div style="margin-bottom:8px;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:.5px solid #1a2030">
            <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;margin-bottom:3px">
              <div style="font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0">LAX to NYC — Actually Perfect</div>
              <div style="font-family:'Syne',sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--teal)">9.1</div>
            </div>
            <div style="font-size:11px;color:#3a5070">by SkyTraveler22 · 2h ago · Gate agents were extraordinary...</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;margin-bottom:3px">
              <div style="font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0">The Boarding Nightmare</div>
              <div style="font-family:'Syne',sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--coral)">2.4</div>
            </div>
            <div style="font-size:11px;color:#3a5070">by PinkWagon77 · 5h ago · No announcement for 45 min...</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="phone-tab-bar">
          <div class="phone-tab">Home</div>
          <div class="phone-tab">Explore</div>
          <div class="phone-tab active" style="color:var(--pink)">+</div>
          <div class="phone-tab active" style="color:var(--pink)">Brands</div>
          <div class="phone-tab">Profile</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<!-- SCREEN 4: B2B INTELLIGENCE DASHBOARD                    -->
<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="wf-screen">
  <div class="wf-header">
    <div class="wf-title">Screen 04 — Business Intelligence Dashboard</div>
    <div class="wf-num">The B2B Payoff</div>
  </div>
  <div class="wf-desc">The dashboard that CEOs actually open — because the data is proprietary and unavailable anywhere else. Every story from the consumer side flows in here in real time. What Meltwater charges $30,000/year for, BISS delivers at $50–$800/month.</div>
  <div class="wf-body">
    <div class="desktop-frame">
      <div class="desktop-bar">
        <div class="desktop-dots">
          <div class="desktop-dot" style="background:#ff5f57"></div>
          <div class="desktop-dot" style="background:#febc2e"></div>
          <div class="desktop-dot" style="background:#28c840"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="url-bar">biss.io/dashboard/southwest-airlines</div>
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:160px 1fr;height:560px">
        <!-- Sidebar -->
        <div style="background:#040810;border-right:1px solid #0d1a2e;padding:16px 12px">
          <div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:var(--pink);letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:20px;padding:0 4px">BISS</div>
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:#3a5070;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:8px;padding:0 4px">Southwest Air</div>
          <div style="margin-bottom:4px">
            <div style="background:#0d1a2e;border-radius:6px;padding:7px 10px;font-size:12px;color:var(--teal);font-weight:500">Dashboard</div>
          </div>
          <div style="padding:7px 10px;font-size:12px;color:#3a5070;cursor:pointer">Stories</div>
          <div style="padding:7px 10px;font-size:12px;color:#3a5070">Trends</div>
          <div style="padding:7px 10px;font-size:12px;color:#3a5070">Seeds</div>
          <div style="padding:7px 10px;font-size:12px;color:#3a5070">Competitors</div>
          <div style="padding:7px 10px;font-size:12px;color:#3a5070">Reports</div>
        </div>
        <!-- Main dashboard -->
        <div style="background:#060e1c;padding:20px;overflow:auto">
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:16px">
            <div>
              <div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0">Southwest Airlines · Intelligence Dashboard</div>
              <div style="font-size:11px;color:#3a5070">Last 30 days · 847 stories analyzed</div>
            </div>
            <div style="background:#0d1a2e;border:.5px solid #1a2a3a;border-radius:6px;padding:5px 12px;font-size:11px;color:#647a96">Export Report ↓</div>
          </div>
          <!-- Metrics row -->
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px;margin-bottom:16px">
            <div class="dash-metric"><div class="dash-num">4.2</div><div style="font-size:9px;color:var(--teal);margin-top:2px">↑ +0.3</div><div class="dash-label">Sentiment</div></div>
            <div class="dash-metric"><div class="dash-num">847</div><div style="font-size:9px;color:var(--teal);margin-top:2px">↑ +124</div><div class="dash-label">Stories</div></div>
            <div class="dash-metric"><div class="dash-num gold">73%</div><div style="font-size:9px;color:var(--gold);margin-top:2px">boarding</div><div class="dash-label">Pain Score</div></div>
            <div class="dash-metric"><div class="dash-num">48</div><div style="font-size:9px;color:var(--teal);margin-top:2px">↑ +2</div><div class="dash-label">NPS Proxy</div></div>
          </div>
          <!-- Chart + AI insight row -->
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 200px;gap:12px;margin-bottom:16px">
            <div style="background:#0d1830;border:1px solid #1a3050;border-radius:8px;padding:12px">
              <div style="font-size:11px;color:#3a5070;margin-bottom:8px">Sentiment Trend</div>
              <!-- Simple SVG chart -->
              <svg width="100%" height="60" viewBox="0 0 300 60">
                <polyline points="0,45 50,40 100,35 150,42 200,28 250,22 300,18" fill="none" stroke="#00C4A7" stroke-width="2"/>
                <polyline points="0,48 50,50 100,52 150,49 200,47 250,50 300,48" fill="none" stroke="#1A3355" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4,3"/>
                <text x="0" y="58" font-size="9" fill="#3a5070">Jan</text>
                <text x="130" y="58" font-size="9" fill="#3a5070">Mar</text>
                <text x="270" y="58" font-size="9" fill="#3a5070">May</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div style="background:#0f1a00;border:1px solid #2a3a00;border-radius:8px;padding:12px">
              <div style="font-size:10px;color:var(--gold);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:6px">AI Insight</div>
              <div style="font-size:12px;color:#e8e8f0;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:8px">Boarding communication flagged in <strong style="color:var(--gold)">73%</strong> of delay stories. Priority fix recommended.</div>
              <div style="background:#1a2a00;border-radius:4px;padding:5px 8px;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--gold)">→ View all insights</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- Pain points -->
          <div style="background:#0d1830;border:1px solid #1a3050;border-radius:8px;padding:12px">
            <div style="font-size:11px;color:#3a5070;margin-bottom:10px">Top Pain Points</div>
            <div class="pain-item"><div class="pain-label"><span>Boarding delays</span><span style="color:var(--gold)">73%</span></div><div class="pain-track"><div class="pain-fill" style="width:73%"></div></div></div>
            <div class="pain-item"><div class="pain-label"><span>App reliability</span><span>58%</span></div><div class="pain-track"><div class="pain-fill" style="width:58%"></div></div></div>
            <div class="pain-item"><div class="pain-label"><span>Communication</span><span>40%</span></div><div class="pain-track"><div class="pain-fill" style="width:40%"></div></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<!-- SCREEN 5: DISCOVER / COMMUNITY FEED                     -->
<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="wf-screen">
  <div class="wf-header">
    <div class="wf-title">Screen 05 — Discover / Community Feed</div>
    <div class="wf-num">The Word-of-Mouth Layer</div>
  </div>
  <div class="wf-desc">Not an algorithm pushing strangers' content. Experiences from people you already follow surface first — friends, colleagues, creators whose judgment you'd actually ask for in real life. The Parallel Universe feature lets users see the road not taken: "You flew United. What if you had chosen Southwest?"</div>
  <div class="wf-body">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:start">
      <div class="phone-outer">
        <div class="phone-frame">
          <div class="phone-status"><span>9:41</span><span>🔋</span></div>
          <div class="phone-nav">
            <span style="font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:var(--pink)">BISS</span>
            <span style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0">Discover</span>
            <span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--teal)">🔍</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Filter tabs -->
          <div style="display:flex;gap:0;border-bottom:.5px solid #1e2030;padding:0 14px">
            <div style="padding:8px 12px;font-size:12px;background:#00C4A7;color:#0a1628;font-weight:600;border-radius:20px 20px 0 0;margin-bottom:-1px">All</div>
            <div style="padding:8px 12px;font-size:12px;color:#3a5070">Travel</div>
            <div style="padding:8px 12px;font-size:12px;color:#3a5070">Food</div>
            <div style="padding:8px 12px;font-size:12px;color:#3a5070;font-weight:600;color:var(--teal)">Friends ★</div>
          </div>
          <!-- Feed items -->
          <div style="padding:12px 14px">
            <!-- Item 1 — positive -->
            <div class="feed-item" style="margin-bottom:10px">
              <div class="feed-user">
                <div class="feed-avatar" style="background:var(--teal)">JM</div>
                <div style="flex:1">
                  <div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0">Jordan M. <span style="color:#3a5070;font-weight:400">· Following</span></div>
                  <div style="font-size:10px;color:#3a5070">Southwest Airlines · 2h ago</div>
                </div>
                <div class="feed-score-badge" style="background:#1a3020;color:var(--teal);border:.5px solid var(--teal-dk)">9.1</div>
              </div>
              <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0;margin-bottom:4px">LAX to NYC — Actually Perfect</div>
              <div style="font-size:11.5px;color:#647a96;margin-bottom:8px">Gate agents were extraordinary. Boarded on time, staff checked in mid-flight...</div>
              <div class="one-word-pills">
                <div class="owp" style="background:#1a3020;border-color:#2a4030;color:var(--teal)">Same!</div>
                <div class="owp">Jealous</div>
                <div class="owp">Helpful</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <!-- Item 2 — negative -->
            <div class="feed-item">
              <div class="feed-user">
                <div class="feed-avatar" style="background:var(--purple)">AK</div>
                <div style="flex:1">
                  <div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0">Alex K. <span style="color:#3a5070;font-weight:400">· Following</span></div>
                  <div style="font-size:10px;color:#3a5070">Airbnb · Paris · 4h ago</div>
                </div>
                <div class="feed-score-badge" style="background:#2a1a1a;color:#F97066;border:.5px solid #4a2020">3.8</div>
              </div>
              <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0;margin-bottom:4px">Marais Apartment — Skip It</div>
              <div style="font-size:11.5px;color:#647a96;margin-bottom:8px">Photos didn't match reality at all. Host unresponsive on check-in day...</div>
              <!-- Parallel Universe tease -->
              <div style="background:#0a1220;border:.5px solid #1a2a3a;border-radius:8px;padding:8px 10px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px">
                <span style="font-size:16px">↔</span>
                <div>
                  <div style="font-size:10.5px;color:var(--teal);font-weight:600">Parallel Universe</div>
                  <div style="font-size:10.5px;color:#3a5070">What if Alex had stayed at Hotel des Grands Boulevards instead?</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Annotations -->
      <div style="padding:8px 0">
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px"><span style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--purple);color:var(--dark);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0">1</span><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--white)">Trusted Social Graph</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding-left:34px">"Friends ★" tab surfaces only stories from people you follow — not anonymous strangers. This is the word-of-mouth engine: the most powerful travel recommendation is still a friend saying "I just flew Southwest and it was perfect."</div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px"><span style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--purple);color:var(--dark);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0">2</span><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--white)">The Parallel Universe</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding-left:34px">BISS's signature discovery feature. "You flew United and had a nightmare. What if you had chosen Southwest?" Surfaces authentic community data about the road not taken — the experience you didn't have, through the eyes of people who did.</div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--card2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:12px 14px">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:600;color:var(--purple);letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px">Design philosophy</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7">Not an algorithm — a social graph.<br>Not anonymous strangers — people you follow.<br>Not disappearing in 24h — permanent, indexed.<br>Not a like count — a one-word emotional response.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<!-- SCREEN 6: CONTEST / SEEDED QUESTION FLOW               -->
<!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="wf-screen">
  <div class="wf-header">
    <div class="wf-title">Screen 06 — Contest &amp; Seeded Question Flow</div>
    <div class="wf-num">The Creative Market · The Third Business Model</div>
  </div>
  <div class="wf-desc">Any brand or public figure can seed a question or creative challenge to the BISS audience. The Taylor Swift album naming example shows the celebrity flywheel in action: she seeds a question, her audience arrives at BISS to respond, new users are now inside the platform permanently.</div>
  <div class="wf-body">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:start">
      <div class="phone-outer">
        <div class="phone-frame">
          <div class="phone-status"><span>9:41</span><span>🔋</span></div>
          <div class="phone-nav">
            <span style="font-size:13px;color:#555">← Back</span>
            <span style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0">Active Challenge</span>
            <span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--gold)">Share</span>
          </div>
          <div style="padding:14px;background:#0d1117">
            <!-- Contest prompt card -->
            <div class="contest-prompt">
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-bottom:10px">
                <div style="width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--gold);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:14px;color:var(--dark);font-weight:800">TS</div>
                <div>
                  <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0">Taylor Swift</div>
                  <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:4px"><span style="font-size:10px;color:var(--gold)">✓ Verified Creator</span></div>
                </div>
                <div style="margin-left:auto;font-size:10px;color:#3a5070">23h left</div>
              </div>
              <div style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0;margin-bottom:8px;line-height:1.4">"Help me name my next album. Tell me what the title means to you — and why."</div>
              <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:11px;color:#3a5070">
                <span>🖊 47,832 entries</span>
                <span>🏆 Prize: Signed vinyl + meet &amp; greet</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <!-- Entries -->
            <div style="font-size:10px;color:#3a5070;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:8px">Top entries · Community voting</div>
            <div class="contest-entry">
              <div style="font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0;margin-bottom:4px">"The Tortured Poets Department II"</div>
              <div style="font-size:11.5px;color:#647a96;margin-bottom:6px;line-height:1.5">Because your poetry has always been about surviving — and this era feels like the aftermath of survival...</div>
              <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center">
                <span style="font-size:10px;color:#3a5070">by MidnightRavenXX</span>
                <div class="contest-vote-bar">
                  <div class="contest-vote" style="color:var(--teal);border-color:var(--teal-dk);background:#0a2020">Same!</div>
                  <div class="contest-vote" style="color:#647a96;border-color:#1a3050">✓</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="contest-entry">
              <div style="font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:#e8e8f0;margin-bottom:4px">"Folklore II: The Long Game"</div>
              <div style="font-size:11.5px;color:#647a96;margin-bottom:6px;line-height:1.5">Folklore felt like a secret. This one should feel like it was always coming...</div>
              <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center">
                <span style="font-size:10px;color:#3a5070">by StargazerKai</span>
                <div class="contest-vote-bar">
                  <div class="contest-vote" style="color:var(--purple);border-color:#4a4e8a;background:#0a0a20">Iconic</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <!-- CTA -->
            <div style="background:var(--teal);border-radius:10px;padding:12px;text-align:center;margin-top:10px">
              <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#0a1628">Write Your Entry</div>
              <div style="font-size:11px;color:#0a1628;opacity:.7;margin-top:2px">Tell Taylor what the title means to you</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Annotations -->
      <div style="padding:8px 0">
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px"><span style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--gold);color:var(--dark);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0">1</span><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--white)">Verified Creator Account</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding-left:34px">Taylor Swift is a paying Verified Creator subscriber — she gets a gold tick, analytics on all responses, and priority placement in discovery. This is one of the contest platform's four revenue streams.</div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px"><span style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--gold);color:var(--dark);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0">2</span><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--white)">Stories, Not Votes</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding-left:34px">47,832 entries — each one a story explaining WHY, not just a click. Instagram would return a vote count. BISS returns 47,832 narratives that Taylor can actually read, share with her team, and use to understand her audience at a depth no poll delivers.</div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px"><span style="width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--gold);color:var(--dark);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0">3</span><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--white)">One-Word Community Voting</span></div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding-left:34px">The BISS one-word response system applies to contest entries too — "Same!", "Iconic", "Obvious." Creates social signal on submissions without turning into a combative comments section.</div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#0f1a00;border:1px solid #2a3a00;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 14px">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:600;color:var(--gold);letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px">The flywheel in action</div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7">Taylor seeds the question → her Swifties come to BISS → they write entries, create accounts → they discover journal entries, brand pages, other contests → they stay. Taylor's audience becomes BISS's audience. She's a customer AND an acquisition channel.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

